In considering all the various trite attempts at humor I could compose, 
I stumbled upon a YANI:

If Izchak dies, the entire dungeon goes dark. Light spells and sources 
are effective at half of normal for the rest of the game.

If Izchak is killed by direct action, the entire dungeon goes dark; and, 
light spells and sources are effective at 25% of normal for the rest of 
the game.

If you happen to restore Izchak back to life, the darkness is abated.




